        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "Determine the solution set of the system of inequalities \\(\\begin{cases}\\sqrt{x+3}\\geq x\\sqrt{x+3}\\leq x+1\\end{cases}\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The first inequality, considering the domain \\(x\\geq -3\\), gives \\(x\\leq 3\\). For the second inequality, \\(x+1\\geq 0\\) is necessary; squaring then gives \\(x+3\\leq (x+1)^2\\), or \\((x+2)(x-1)\\geq 0\\). Thus \\(x\\geq 1\\). The intersection is \\(\\left[1,3\\right]\\).",
